id: pm-vcs-simi
title: Investigate intermittent uninspectable payload refusal in publication erasure setup
description: "During the full Bun-invoked release check at e03471b, test/publication-validation.test.ts:143 failed at its initial repo.obliterate call on line 147, before the fresh binary staging assertions. The scanner raised uninspectable_payload: Recognizable zlib data cannot be completely inspected. The stack reaches control metadata inspection in engine/erasure.ts:174 and engine/representations.ts:29. The test and both engine files are unchanged from origin/main. That run passed 1540/1541 tests with no skips and all-source per-file 100% coverage. The corresponding complete npm release check passed 1541/1541. A focused reproduction passed 1/1 and the complete publication-validation file passed 7/7. The offending bytes were not retained by fixture cleanup, so the exact cause remains unproven. Investigate generated control metadata and representation recognition without relaxing fail-closed inspection, thresholds, or skips."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: erasure,testing
created_at: "2026-10-15T21:04:31.257Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T07:58:33.018Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Identify and retain a sanitized deterministic reproducer; preserve conservative erasure refusals; stabilize the fixture only with an independently failing behavioral proof.
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T21:06:53.529Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up only: scanner and publication test are byte-identical to origin/main. The failure stack is in eraseFile control-file inspection, before the binary staging assertions. Focused reproduction passed 1/1; full publication-validation file passed 7/7. Do not infer a Bun runtime defect: the failed Bun-invoked release command executes this test through Node. Preserve fail-closed behavior; the specific offending control bytes were not retained, and a generated-metadata interaction is an unconfirmed hypothesis."
  "2026-10-15T21:35:33.467Z",codex-agent,"Discovered while validating pm-vcs-00mb, pm-vcs-sl77 and pm-vcs-w3yi. The unchanged complete Bun release retry at e03471b exited 0: 1541/1541 passed, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo, all 65 source files at per-file 100% coverage. The original control-metadata inspection refusal remains unexplained; focused success and a full retry do not remediate it. Keep this follow-up open; no scanner, publication test, safety bound or threshold was changed."
  "2026-10-18T04:23:07.287Z",codex-agent,"A deterministic instance of this failure class is retained: decimal PID text beginning with 80 satisfies the zlib header recognition test. The exact current writer PID is typed lock metadata, inspected for raw and canonical base64 aliases, while changed lock contents and all other control files retain complete representation inspection. Tests retain refusals for raw/base64 selected-byte aliases, compressed selected bytes in a changed lock, and an 80-prefixed value in unrelated control metadata. Focused regression passes 1/1. Reverting only eraseFile to origin/main makes the same test fail 0/1 with uninspectable_payload; source imports require no dist rebuild. Earlier CI bytes/PIDs were not retained, so this proves a failure mode without claiming the original PID. Global scanner bounds and untrusted-payload refusals are unchanged. Both linked commands passed after reviewing and locally acknowledging the historical command provenance; the initial trust refusal was not treated as a passing test."
  "2026-10-19T23:44:48.962Z",codex-agent,"PR 131 acceptance uncovered another deterministic instance in known orphan-owner metadata. In a disposable real native repository: set erase authority, commit a synthetic payload, create control file objects.lock.801234.0123456789ab.tmp containing decimal text 801234, then obliterate the payload. Current code refuses uninspectable_payload: Recognizable zlib data cannot be completely inspected. Replacing only the retained orphan file text with 901234 lets the same erasure complete. engine/erasure.ts only treats the exact live objects.lock PID as typed metadata; the supported orphan-owner filename is scanned as an arbitrary representation. During the concurrent Bun-invoked full gate, unchanged composition test review atomic publication preserves native permission failures and known orphan owner metadata failed once, while npm and an independent focused run passed. Full-run assertion detail is still pending, so this synthetic repro is not a claim about that exact process PID. No erasure safety checks, timing, assertions or thresholds changed in the review patch."
  "2026-10-19T23:45:38.142Z",codex-agent,"The failed acceptance runner flushed its assertion detail when interrupted: composition.test.ts:1133 repo.obliterate raised uninspectable_payload through engine/erasure.ts:190 and engine/representations.ts:29, after the native permission assertions had passed. This confirms the same control-metadata inspection failure class, not a permission-race assertion failure. The original orphan bytes/PID were removed by fixture cleanup, so the exact original PID remains unproven. The failed Bun attempt was stopped after this known failure; cancellation/partial-coverage results are not acceptance. A complete unchanged serial retry is required. The deterministic synthetic 801234 orphan-owner repro above remains reproducible without relaxing inspection."
  "2026-10-20T00:22:35.697Z",codex-agent,"The unchanged complete Bun-invoked release retry passed 1709/1709, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo, with per-file 100 percent coverage across all 70 production files and all remaining acceptance checks passing. The matching composition test passed both in isolation (1/1) and in that complete retry; its command is linked here. The independent synthetic 801234 orphan-owner repro is still a real uninspectable_payload refusal, and passing acceptance does not remediate it. This follow-up remains in progress; no erasure code, safety check, timing or test assertion was changed. Releasing the evidence-only claim."
  "2026-10-23T07:58:30.286Z",codex-agent,"PR 144 CI run 39919162579, Node 22 npm gate, again failed composition.test.ts review atomic publication preserves native permission failures and known orphan owner metadata at its initial obliterate call. Stack: engine/representations.ts:29 through engine/erasure.ts:190; code uninspectable_payload, Recognizable zlib data cannot be completely inspected. This is the already retained orphan-owner metadata failure class. Original offending PID/bytes were not retained, so this does not identify their exact value. The same test passed in the earlier full run and in an independent focused retry (1/1). Node 26 passed its complete npm gate at the same head. No erasure scanner, refusal, timing, safety check or threshold was changed; this issue remains unresolved."
